 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::execute_slash_command` runs a backend-owned slash command against an existing
+  agent session without treating the command as an ordinary user prompt. The default implementation
+  returns a provider-neutral unsupported-command message without sending a model request.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
+- `AgentBackend::execute_slash_command_streaming` provides real-time output for backend-owned slash
+  commands. Its default implementation calls `execute_slash_command`.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
   `AgentBackend::send_streaming_interruptible` extend the streaming calls with a provider-neutral
   stop detector. Providers that can interrupt an in-flight turn use the detector to stop generation
@@ -227,6 +232,8 @@ public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can parti
   provider-neutral session state. The complete transcript is used for orchestrator directive parsing
   even when the app-server reports several assistant message items before the final turn-completed
   notification.
+- `CodexBackend::execute_slash_command_streaming` dispatches selected-agent slash commands through
+  the app-server command channel, preserves the Codex thread id, and records returned token usage.
 - Codex linearizer sessions run with the dedicated linearize sandbox, which defaults to
   `workspace-write` and can be configured with `WORK_LEAF_CODEX_LINEARIZE_SANDBOX` (`read-only`,
   `workspace-write`, or `danger-full-access`). The approval policy remains `never`. Patch agents and
@@ -654,9 +661,10 @@ New agent-provider support follows this path:
 1. Define an `AgentProfile` with `AgentKind::External`.
 2. Implement `AgentBackend` for the provider.
 3. Override streaming methods when the provider can emit real-time output.
-4. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
-5. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
-6. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
+4. Override slash-command methods when the provider owns selected-agent command actions.
+5. Return an `AgentShutdownHandle` when the provider owns child processes.
+6. Pass the profile through `CommandChat::with_agent_profile`.
+7. Use `WorkLeafController` or `CommandChat` without modifying terminal UI code.
 
 `AgentBackend::session` is an optional session snapshot hook. Work Leaf tracks hidden system-agent
 initialization itself, so provider implementations do not need to override `session` for persistent
